//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai, peano
//
// Dynamic CONDITIONAL passthrough on real hardware. The runtime sequence guards
// the whole n-tile transfer with a runtime i1 %do_copy; when false it issues no
// DMAs and the output stays untouched. The scf.if nests the rolled ping-pong
// scf.for, both lowered through the dynamic BD free-list pool (the static
// allocator would reject the runtime control flow). One xclbin serves any
// (n, do_copy): the instruction stream is built at runtime by the generated C++
// TXN builder called with both.
//
// aiecc builds both the xclbin and the parameterized instruction builder.
// The host #includes that header and calls it per (n, do_copy).
//
// RUN: mkdir -p %t.prj
// RUN: cp %S/aie.mlir aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %run_on_npu1% sed 's/NPUDEVICE/npu1_1col/g' -i aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% sed 's/NPUDEVICE/npu2_1col/g' -i aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %aiecc --get-xclbin --get-npu-cpp --npu-cpp-name=%t.gen.h \
// RUN:   --output-dir=%t.prj \
// RUN:   --xclbin-name=%t.xclbin --tmpdir=%t.prj aie_arch.mlir
//
// RUN: %host_clang %S/test.cpp -o %t.exe -std=c++17 -Wall \
// RUN:   -DGEN_HDR='"%t.gen.h"' -DXCLBIN='std::string("%/t.xclbin")' \
// RUN:   -I%S/../../../include %xrt_flags %host_link_flags %test_utils_flags
//
// argv: [n] [do_copy]. Exercise the taken branch (do_copy=1) at a couple of tile
// counts and the not-taken branch (do_copy=0, output untouched). The host
// returns non-zero on mismatch, so lit checks the exit code directly.
// RUN: %run_on_npu1% %t.exe 2 1
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% %t.exe 2 1
// RUN: %run_on_npu1% %t.exe 8 1
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% %t.exe 8 1
// RUN: %run_on_npu1% %t.exe 8 0
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% %t.exe 8 0
